threads.body:
[General] Same story for this block — it is copied verbatim from `v1_4/AbstractRpcClientInstrumentation.CallMethodAdvice.onEnter` (same unshaded `ClientProtos`, same `HbaseBatchMetadata`, same `HbaseRequest.create` argument order). Only the `shouldStart`/`start` part below is actually version-specific. Since `HbaseClientUtil` is being introduced in the common module anyway, this is a natural fit for it:

```java
  public static HbaseRequest createRequest(
      Object md, Object param, User ticket, InetSocketAddress addr) {
    String operation = methodDescriptorName(md);
    Long batchSize = null;
    if (emitStableDatabaseSemconv() && param instanceof ClientProtos.MultiRequest) {
      HbaseBatchMetadata batchMetadata =
          HbaseBatchMetadata.create((ClientProtos.MultiRequest) param);
      operation = batchMetadata.getOperation();
      batchSize = batchMetadata.getOperationBatchSize();
    }
    return HbaseRequest.create(
        operation,
        getTableName(),
        ticket.getName(),
        addr.getHostString(),
        addr.getPort(),
        batchSize);
  }
```

Otherwise the two copies will silently drift the next time the batch/semconv handling changes.

